.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
.Dd November 13, 2026
.Dt NOQTIS-DATA 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm noqtis-data
.Nd make, show and check a capsule's data record
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm noqtis data init
.Op Fl f | Fl -force
.Ar dir
.Nm noqtis data add
.Op Fl u | Fl -url Ar url
.Op Fl -title Ar text
.Op Fl -publisher Ar text
.Op Fl -licence Ar text
.Op Fl -retrieved Ar time | Cm now
.Op Fl -etag Ar text
.Op Fl -modified Ar text
.Op Fl -archived Ar url
.Op Fl -mirror Ar url ...
.Op Fl -synthetic
.Ar dir file ...
.Nm noqtis data put
.Ar dir member json-file | Cm -
.Nm noqtis data del
.Ar dir member
.Op Ar path | name
.Nm noqtis data fmt
.Ar dir
.Nm noqtis data show
.Op Fl j | Fl -json
.Ar dir
.Nm noqtis data check
.Op Fl j | Fl -json
.Ar dir
.Nm noqtis data syn
.Fl -seed Ar n
.Op Fl -rows Ar n
.Ar dir file
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The data record,
.Pa noqtis.data.json
in a capsule folder
.Pq Xr noqtis-data 5 ,
says where each data file came from, its schema and summaries, and the
steps and checks made with it.
It is a file of the capsule like any other: seal the folder
.Pq Xr noqtis-seal 1
after changing the record, and the seal covers it.
Each command that changes the record of a sealed folder says so.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm init
Writes a record that holds only its format.
.Fl f
replaces a record that is there.
.It Cm add
Records the SHA-256 and size of each
.Ar file
(a path in
.Ar dir ,
.Ql /
between folders) as a source, keeping what the record already says of
it, so a file fetched again keeps its URL.
A folder with no record gets a new one.
The options describe where one file came from:
.Fl -url ,
.Fl -title ,
.Fl -publisher ,
.Fl -licence ,
.Fl -retrieved
(a UTC time
.Ql YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ ,
or
.Cm now :
the clock, or
.Ev SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH
when set),
.Fl -etag
and
.Fl -modified
(the server's ETag and Last-Modified),
.Fl -archived
(the URL of an archived copy),
.Fl -mirror
(another URL with the same bytes, up to 32), and
.Fl -synthetic
(the file is a generated stand-in: every report line about it says so).
.It Cm put
Adds the element in
.Ar json-file
.Pf ( Cm -
for standard input) to
.Ar member :
.Cm sources ,
.Cm schemas ,
.Cm stats ,
.Cm chunks
(replacing the element with the same path),
.Cm checks
(the same name),
.Cm steps ,
.Cm commits
(appended), or sets
.Cm env
or
.Cm cite .
The element is checked as the format defines it; a refusal names the
member and what is wrong.
.It Cm del
Removes the element of
.Ar member
with that path or name, or the whole member.
.It Cm fmt
Reads a record edited by hand (any member order, keyed arrays in any
order) and writes it in canonical form.
.It Cm show
Prints the record, one element a line;
.Fl j
prints it as it is.
.It Cm check
Checks the record: that it is canonical and of the format, that each
source file is there with its recorded SHA-256 and size, that each
schema's file matches it, that each file's summaries
.Pq Xr noqtis-drift 1
are made again the same from it, that the script or mapping of each
step that names one with its SHA-256 still has it, and that no
recorded check failed: one with
.Cm expected
and
.Cm observed
numbers is recomputed against its
.Cm tol
(0 when not given), one with strings must have them equal, and one
recorded as
.Ql pass
that does not hold fails.
It prints one row per check and, on standard error, what to do about
each kind of failure.
.Fl j
prints one line of JSON:
.Bd -literal
{"folder":"<dir>","ok":<bool>,"checks":[{"check":"<name>",
 "ok":<bool>,"detail":"<text>"[,"fix":"<text>"]},...]}
.Ed
.It Cm syn
Writes a synthetic
.Ar file
in
.Ar dir
from the record's schema of it, the recipe (columns, types, ranges,
sets, missing values, delimiter, header), with
.Fl -rows
rows (default the schema's
.Cm rows.min ,
else 100), the same bytes for the same
.Fl -seed
(required, from 0 to 2^64 \- 1), and records it as a source marked
.Cm synthetic ,
so every check of it says
.Ql [synthetic] .
It never writes in place of a file the record does not mark synthetic.
.Xr nqdsyn 3
defines the values.
.El
.Pp
.Cm noqtis data check
does not check the seal, and
.Xr noqtis-check 1
does not read the record: run both.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH
the time
.Fl -retrieved Cm now
records, in seconds since 1970
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It 0
success; for
.Cm check ,
every check passed
.It 1
.Cm check :
a check failed
.It 2
a usage or file error, or a record that is not valid
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ noqtis data add --url https://example.org/a.csv \e
    --retrieved now results data/a.csv
$ noqtis data check results
      check   detail
ok    record  noqtis-data-1, canonical: 1 sources, 0 schemas
ok    source  data/a.csv: SHA-256 and size match
results: OK (2 checks passed)
$ noqtis seal -k key results
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-check 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-seal 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-src 1 ,
.Xr nqdchk 3 ,
.Xr nqdnew 3 ,
.Xr noqtis-data 5
